      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Wrong? No—it's the most human thing in the world to want the pain to end. But you're not ending the pain, you're just ending yourself, and he's not waiting on the other side—he's gone, and you're still here, breathing, aching, alive. That's not weakness; that's the cruelest kind of punishment, and you're already surviving it. So if you're going to stay, stay angry, stay stubborn, stay for the spite—but don't mistake a permanent exit for a reunion that will never come.",
